  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/analyze_flame_pressure.py",
    "old_str": "print(\"\\nAnalysis complete. Results saved to outputs/ and report/images/\")",
    "new_str": "print(\"\\nAnalysis complete. Results saved to ../outputs/ and ../report/images/\")"
  }
}
```

Now let me run the script again to generate the images.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "cd code && python analyze_flame_pressure.py"
  }
}
```

Good! Now let me check if the images and outputs were created.

```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir report\\images"
  }
}
```


```json
{
  "tool": "run_shell",
  "args": {
    "cmd": "dir outputs"
  }
}
```

Great! The deeper analysis provides more insights:
1. There's a statistically significant difference between flame speeds in low vs high pressure regions (p=0.0042)
2. The high pressure region actually has higher average flame speed (30.76 cm/s) than low pressure region (27.63 cm/s)
3. Residuals from the piecewise model are not normally distributed (Shapiro-Wilk p=4.7e-10)

Now let me check if all the new images were created.

```json
